1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,378
[BILLY] <i>Do you know what caused the fire?</i>

2
00:00:03,461 --> 00:00:05,338
[CLERK] <i>No one knows, miss.</i>

3
00:00:05,422 --> 00:00:08,758
<i>All I heard was that Mariela survived.</i>

4
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:10,552
<i>And so did her youngest daughter.</i>

5
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:12,804
<i>But her eldest daughter died.</i>

6
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:14,556
[JORDAN] <i>When did the fire happen?</i>

7
00:00:14,639 --> 00:00:18,226
[CLERK] <i>About 12 to 13 years ago, I think.</i>

8
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:20,854
[BILLY] <i>But the father</i>
<i>wasn't with them?</i>

9
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:22,689
[CLERK] <i>No,</i>
<i>he wasn't.</i>

10
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:26,317
<i>The rumor is that</i>
<i>Mariela's husband left her.</i>

11
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:32,323
<i>You sure about this, Billy?</i>

12
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:34,492
<i>You don't want Oliver to go home for now?</i>

13
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,537
<i>He's growing up, Auntie Pres.</i>

14
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:39,330
<i>You okay with this?</i>

15
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:40,582
<i>For now.</i>

16
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:45,211
<i>Look how happy he was with his dad.</i>

17
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:49,591
<i>Dear.</i>

18
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,594
<i>- Ma.</i>
<i>- Where's your laundry?</i>

19
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:55,138
[BEA] <i>No need. I'll do it myself.</i>

20
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:57,432
[MARIELA] <i>Let me do it. Just go to work.</i>

21
00:00:57,515 --> 00:01:04,230
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

22
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,526
<i>How do you do that?</i>

23
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:11,362
<i>Compartmentalizing.</i>

24
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:13,740
<i>It's like you don't even think about…</i>

25
00:01:13,823 --> 00:01:15,075
<i>About what?</i>

26
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:16,534
<i>About Oliver.</i>

27
00:01:16,618 --> 00:01:17,577
<i>Hmm.</i>

28
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,871
<i>I just didn't expect that</i>

29
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:21,372
<i>you'd let him.</i>

30
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:23,666
<i>I just gave Oliver what--</i>

31
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,543
<i>What he wanted?</i>

32
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:27,295
<i>What he needed.</i>

33
00:01:27,378 --> 00:01:29,255
<i>I kept it a secret from him for years.</i>

34
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:33,676
<i>Because I wanted to protect him.</i>

35
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,178
<i>But you know, dude,</i>

36
00:01:35,887 --> 00:01:38,765
<i>when I saw him with that man,</i>

37
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:43,978
<i>I knew I was wrong to decide for Oliver.</i>

38
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:46,773
<i>Because all he wants is to know his dad.</i>

39
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:48,817
<i>Mr. Dino.</i>

40
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:50,527
<i>Good morning.</i>

41
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,988
<i>Why'd you choose to join our group?</i>

42
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:57,742
<i>From what I can see,</i>
<i>you're the nicest people here.</i>

43
00:01:59,035 --> 00:02:00,078
<i>What do you know?</i>

44
00:02:01,246 --> 00:02:02,163
<i>Nothing.</i>

45
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:05,792
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

46
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:07,001
<i>What do you know?</i>

47
00:02:08,086 --> 00:02:09,170
[STAMMERS] <i>N-Nothing.</i>

48
00:02:09,712 --> 00:02:11,339
<i>Is there something I should know?</i>

49
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:16,803
<i>What makes LoveList different</i>

50
00:02:16,886 --> 00:02:18,805
<i>from all the other swipe apps?</i>

51
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:21,933
<i>Good question.</i>

52
00:02:22,016 --> 00:02:24,811
<i>Well, LoveList isn't based on swipes.</i>

53
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:28,606
<i>Our matching engine is driven by</i>
<i>how the users behave online.</i>

54
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:32,277
<i>We focus on behavior, not just profiles.</i>

55
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,362
<i>That's where the real signal is.</i>

56
00:02:34,445 --> 00:02:38,867
<i>After reviewing your proposal</i>
<i>and hearing you talk now,</i>

57
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,160
<i>I'm in.</i>

58
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:42,662
<i>- Great. Great! Thank you.</i>
<i>- All right, thank you.</i>

59
00:02:42,745 --> 00:02:46,249
<i>- Thank you for the trust, Mr. Fabrizio.</i>
<i>- Oh, please, just call me Peter.</i>

60
00:02:46,332 --> 00:02:48,042
- [BILLY]<i> Thank you, Peter.</i>
- [PETER]<i> All right.</i>

61
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:49,961
- [JORDAN]<i> Thank you, Peter.</i>
- [PETER]<i> Of course.</i>

62
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:52,589
<i>Enrico, let's meet. We need to talk.</i>

63
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:54,674
<i>Ah, okay, okay.</i>

64
00:02:54,757 --> 00:02:59,971
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:08,313
"Marj Quinto: Love has no
borders, neither do we!

66
00:03:08,396 --> 00:03:10,398
#LovelistGoesGlobal"

67
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:16,988
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

68
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:33,379
The food here's pretty good, Billy.

69
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:40,887
Hm, here, Billy. Have some.

70
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:43,097
I'm good. Keep eating.

71
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:45,183
Here, do you want to order more?

72
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:47,060
[BILLY] Let's order some more.

73
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:48,144
Um…

74
00:03:48,853 --> 00:03:50,188
dessert?

75
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:53,733
Oh! Can I get the apple crumble?

76
00:03:53,816 --> 00:03:56,569
Please. Once in a while is okay, right?

77
00:03:57,153 --> 00:03:58,780
- Hmm…
- [OLIVER] Please?

78
00:03:59,572 --> 00:04:02,367
But they don't have a sugar-free option.

79
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:05,745
Let's drop by the shop we frequent at
on the way home instead.

80
00:04:05,828 --> 00:04:06,663
Okay?

81
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:13,419
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:04:14,045 --> 00:04:15,004
Billy.

83
00:04:15,672 --> 00:04:17,131
Again, I'm sorry.

84
00:04:18,716 --> 00:04:19,676
Are you okay now?

85
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:21,636
[BILLY] Are you happy?

86
00:04:21,719 --> 00:04:22,804
Yes.

87
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:26,182
But… are you no longer mad?

88
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:32,063
You know that I love you very much, right?

89
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:34,774
So that means

90
00:04:35,441 --> 00:04:38,611
you're gonna let me see Papa again?

91
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:42,532
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

92
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:43,491
Mm.

93
00:04:43,574 --> 00:04:44,867
Thank you, Billy!

94
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:48,204
- Thank you!
- Mmm!

95
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,123
Thank you, thank you!

96
00:04:50,206 --> 00:04:52,834
[OLIVER] I promise you.
I'll do my best in my studies.

97
00:04:52,917 --> 00:04:54,460
I'll get my grades up even higher.

98
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:57,630
Once I graduate,
I'll take care of you and Auntie.

99
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:59,215
Mmm.

100
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:01,092
- [OLIVER] Tight hug! Tighter!
- [BILLY GROANING]

101
00:05:01,175 --> 00:05:02,468
Can I still order?

102
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:04,846
Hmm.

103
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:06,347
- Bro Dude?
- Mm-hmm.

104
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:08,016
Bro Dude!

105
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:09,851
Hm?

106
00:05:09,934 --> 00:05:11,769
Bro Dude, Billy and I are okay now.

107
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:14,397
She let me see Papa again.

108
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:18,901
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

109
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:20,361
Qualified.

110
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:21,821
As long as you two made up.

111
00:05:21,904 --> 00:05:24,032
Yes. Let's eat!

112
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:25,408
- [JORDAN] Let's!
- [OLIVER] Okay.

113
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:28,411
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES PLAYING]

114
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:30,288
Are you gonna order?

115
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:31,622
[JORDAN SIGHS]

116
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:40,590
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

117
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:21,380
I hope you can forgive me, Precious.

118
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:26,594
I never meant to hurt you.

119
00:06:26,677 --> 00:06:29,430
I didn't come here
to listen to your explanation.

120
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:32,517
- But, Pres--
- Listen.

121
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:37,396
Billy agreed. You can meet with Oliver
after his classes are over.

122
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,524
4:30 to 5:30.

123
00:06:40,149 --> 00:06:41,234
You can meet up at your house.

124
00:06:41,317 --> 00:06:43,820
But Billy said I have
to be there too.

125
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:46,948
Is that good with you?

126
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:48,950
Pres…

127
00:06:49,033 --> 00:06:54,956
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

128
00:06:58,584 --> 00:07:00,503
- Hi-yah! Hi-yah!
- [SIX-BUTTONS CLACKING]

129
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:02,421
[JORDAN] Are you sure about your decision?

130
00:07:05,341 --> 00:07:07,176
My brother's all grown up.

131
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,095
And really smart too.

132
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:13,266
I just want to give him the chance

133
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:15,893
to meet his father,
even just for a little while.

134
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:19,147
Then it's up to him
after he gets to know him.

135
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:27,530
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

136
00:07:29,323 --> 00:07:30,700
Hello?!

137
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:33,369
Hello?

138
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:35,746
Sorry. I was just surprised.

139
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,874
You're just so mature in what you said.

140
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:41,294
But really, I wish…

141
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:43,254
I wish I had your courage.

142
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:50,011
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

143
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:52,847
[OLIVER] Ugh, I lost.

144
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:57,435
Jordan, Billy, come on.
Let's play over there. Please.

145
00:07:57,518 --> 00:07:59,103
- Oh, of course!
- Enough with your talking.

146
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:00,062
- Let's go!
- Let's play.

147
00:08:00,146 --> 00:08:01,564
- Come on.
- It's playtime.

148
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:02,732
Last one there is a buzzkill.

149
00:08:06,861 --> 00:08:07,904
I'm really sorry.

150
00:08:07,987 --> 00:08:14,202
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

151
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:19,081
[WOMAN] What the hell?!

152
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:21,501
The road is so wide!
You're blocking the way!

153
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:24,420
- I'm just over here on the side!
- Ugh! Don't you have eyes?!

154
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:25,838
Stop! Just get out of here!

155
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:27,089
- Dang it!
- Idiot!

156
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:28,257
- Come on.
- Idiot!

157
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:29,425
Let's go.

158
00:08:30,134 --> 00:08:35,848
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

159
00:08:51,113 --> 00:08:52,823
[MUSIC STOPS]

160
00:08:52,907 --> 00:08:53,950
Mariela?

161
00:08:56,035 --> 00:08:57,703
I saw my husband.

162
00:08:58,621 --> 00:09:00,873
The one who hasn't contacted me in years.

163
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:04,126
I caught him

164
00:09:05,044 --> 00:09:06,712
with another woman again.

165
00:09:07,338 --> 00:09:09,090
He has a new mistress.

166
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:11,425
[SIGHS] Mariela…

167
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:13,261
She took him away from me!

168
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:16,013
I wanted to kill them!

169
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:20,726
If it wouldn't have meant
leaving my daughter behind,

170
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:23,437
if it wouldn't have landed me in prison,

171
00:09:23,521 --> 00:09:25,773
I would've killed them!

172
00:09:25,856 --> 00:09:29,443
My husband and his lover!

173
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:32,989
Mariela, what you're thinking is wrong.
You can't do that.

174
00:09:34,907 --> 00:09:36,784
What about having an affair
with a married man?

175
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:38,119
Is that right?

176
00:09:38,202 --> 00:09:40,037
Huh? Answer me.

177
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:42,957
What? Mariel, please.

178
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:45,710
I don't understand what you're saying.

179
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:47,962
You'll understand.

180
00:09:48,045 --> 00:09:50,548
I'll make you understand

181
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:52,883
how painful it is.

182
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:57,013
I'll make all of you feel it!

183
00:09:57,096 --> 00:10:01,601
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:03,269
What's going on here?

185
00:10:03,352 --> 00:10:05,187
Ma'am, are you okay?

186
00:10:06,897 --> 00:10:08,816
Ma'am, please leave.

187
00:10:08,899 --> 00:10:09,859
Please.

188
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:16,949
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

189
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:25,082
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

190
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:26,125
Wait, wait!

191
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:27,835
- Step back.
- Hey!

192
00:10:28,502 --> 00:10:31,672
- Hey! Don't let him win!
- Wait.

193
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,257
- I'll do it.
- You take over for now, Billy.

194
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:35,301
- Your turn.
- Let me win, okay!

195
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:36,677
- I can do this.
- Go, go!

196
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:38,054
- [SCREAMS]
- Oh!

197
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:39,764
- [OLIVER] Oh no!
- There!

198
00:10:39,847 --> 00:10:42,224
- Wait! Oh my God!
- Oh!

199
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:44,226
- We're almost there!
- We'll catch up.

200
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:45,227
- No, dude.
- Go, Billy!

201
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:46,187
- Go!
- Wait!

202
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:47,229
- Go!
- Go, go!

203
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:49,190
- Hurry!
- Cheater! Cheater!

204
00:10:49,273 --> 00:10:51,275
[CHEERING]

205
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:53,444
- Yeah! Let's go!
- Let's go!

206
00:10:53,527 --> 00:10:55,821
- Billy! Billy!
- I give up.

207
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:57,615
Okay! Whew, it's hot.

208
00:10:57,698 --> 00:10:58,783
Ugh, okay.

209
00:10:58,866 --> 00:10:59,742
[LAUGHING]

210
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:00,826
- Next game!
- Let's go.

211
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,119
- Next game!
- Next game, come on.

212
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:04,955
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

213
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:07,541
- No!
- [CHEERING]

214
00:11:07,625 --> 00:11:09,043
[BILLY] That's enough.

215
00:11:09,126 --> 00:11:11,796
- [BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [EXCITED, INDISTINCT SHOUTS]

216
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:15,424
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

217
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:17,218
[BILLY] Go, Oliver.

218
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,513
[BILLY] Wow!

219
00:11:20,596 --> 00:11:22,473
[PINS CLATTER]

220
00:11:22,556 --> 00:11:24,350
[CHEERING]

221
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:26,769
- [OLIVER CHEERING]
- [BILLY] Okay!

222
00:11:28,687 --> 00:11:30,481
[INDISTINCT SHOUT]

223
00:11:30,564 --> 00:11:33,192
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

224
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:34,568
- Yes! We won!
- [CHEERING]

225
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:35,736
[SCREAMS]

226
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:38,572
- Amazing!
- [OLIVER GRUNTS]

227
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:41,117
You're so good.

228
00:11:41,659 --> 00:11:43,452
- [JORDAN] Nice one.
- [OLIVER] Strike.

229
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:51,252
<i>♪ I'll hold your hand in the madness ♪</i>

230
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:57,133
<i>♪ Run to me if they cast you aside ♪</i>

231
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,718
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

232
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,720
- Oh, he's done for.
- [JORDAN SINGS]

233
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:03,597
The boss is really in love.

234
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:06,142
He's completely smitten.

235
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:07,518
Yeah, he really is.

236
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:10,563
[SLAPS HANDS TOGETHER]

237
00:12:10,646 --> 00:12:12,440
"To my beautiful Valerie…"

238
00:12:12,523 --> 00:12:15,443
- Hey! Hey!
- Wow!

239
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:16,485
That's for Valerie?

240
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:17,945
Obviously. That's what it says, right?

241
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,738
Guys, whose is this?

242
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:21,866
- Hey! Hey! Hey!
- It's Lover Boy's!

243
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:24,243
Looks like he's going to
try his luck with Valerie.

244
00:12:24,326 --> 00:12:26,620
- [RAIN GUSHING]
- [ROBBIE] No!

245
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:28,664
Oh, what's wrong with that?

246
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:31,625
Bro, if you have feelings for her,

247
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:32,960
just tell her.

248
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:36,630
What's important
is that you're being honest.

249
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:38,132
That's true.

250
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:40,176
- That's right.
- Oh, is that true, boss?

251
00:12:40,968 --> 00:12:42,720
- You go first.
- Hey!

252
00:12:43,345 --> 00:12:44,221
What?

253
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:45,890
Oh, no, no. Uh…

254
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:47,308
You write something here first, boss.

255
00:12:48,517 --> 00:12:50,978
- It should come from your heart.
- Boss, come on.

256
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:54,940
You write songs, don't you?

257
00:12:55,024 --> 00:12:58,611
Maybe you can share your talent
when it comes to words.

258
00:12:58,694 --> 00:13:02,656
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

259
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:03,866
There.

260
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:06,327
"To my beautiful Valerie…"

261
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,370
Yeah, that's all I've written so far.

262
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:09,997
- Add more.
- [CHUCKLES]

263
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:12,541
[ROBBIE] That's all I can think of.

264
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:30,267
[OLIVER]<i> Billy is my hero.</i>

265
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:32,811
<i>When our parents died,</i>

266
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:36,315
<i>Billy worked hard to take care of me,</i>

267
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:39,610
<i>send me to school,</i>
<i>and give me a good life.</i>

268
00:13:40,277 --> 00:13:44,657
<i>She taught me that I should</i>
<i>work hard and be brave.</i>

269
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:47,409
<i>Because Billy never backs down.</i>

270
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:49,662
<i>Especially when it comes to family.</i>

271
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:53,666
<i>So for Billy, I'll work hard too.</i>

272
00:13:53,749 --> 00:13:57,419
<i>So that one day,</i>
<i>I'll be the one to take care of her.</i>

273
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:59,838
<i>And I'll be her hero.</i>

274
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:06,929
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

275
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:09,974
<i>Looks like my enemies backed off, Billy.</i>

276
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:11,600
<i>Yeah. I wonder why.</i>

277
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:13,060
<i>Maybe they're scared of you.</i>

278
00:14:13,143 --> 00:14:14,687
<i>- Maybe they're scared of you.</i>
<i>- Me?!</i>

279
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:16,063
<i>Do I look scary?</i>

280
00:14:16,146 --> 00:14:17,314
<i>Very good!</i>

281
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:21,235
<i>Congratulations!</i>
<i>You win one million pesos!</i>

282
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:22,528
<i>Very good!</i>

283
00:14:22,611 --> 00:14:25,614
<i>Just one million?</i>
<i>It should be five million!</i>

284
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:29,159
<i>- I studied hard, you know.</i>
<i>- It can't be five million!</i>

285
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:32,496
<i>It should actually be 10 million</i>
<i>because I memorized that.</i>

286
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:34,290
<i>- You're our baby.</i>
<i>- Baby.</i>

287
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:36,834
<i>- No! No!</i>
<i>- You're still a baby.</i>

288
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:38,419
<i>- Baby.</i>
<i>- Smells like a baby.</i>

289
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:40,254
<i>- No, no, no!</i>
<i>- You're our baby.</i>

290
00:14:40,337 --> 00:14:41,463
<i>- Right?</i>
<i>- No!</i>

291
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:43,674
<i>- You're still a baby.</i>
<i>- I'm not a baby!</i>

292
00:14:43,757 --> 00:14:45,384
<i>- Drink your water, baby.</i>
<i>- No!</i>

293
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:51,849
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

294
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:02,234
Lydia, thank you for coming with me.

295
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:05,029
I didn't want to bother Billy anymore.

296
00:15:05,112 --> 00:15:07,781
Are you really sure about this?

297
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,868
I just want to understand

298
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:14,079
what Mariela and her daughter
are going through.

299
00:15:14,663 --> 00:15:17,625
Well, why don't they try to understand

300
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:20,169
what you and Billy
are going through instead?

301
00:15:20,252 --> 00:15:22,963
Lydia, we're from the Angels of Grace.

302
00:15:23,047 --> 00:15:25,799
We need to be more understanding.

303
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:29,053
I think this might also be a good chance

304
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:33,057
to find out why
they are so angry with Billy.

305
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:40,022
So you think this can still be resolved
with talking and counseling?

306
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:43,233
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

307
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:45,527
Mariela?

308
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:48,238
Bea?

309
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:50,240
Let's just leave.

310
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:51,241
Wait a minute.

311
00:15:51,325 --> 00:15:52,326
Mariela?

312
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:55,245
Mariela?

313
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:57,998
Bea?

314
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,668
Sis, let's just leave.

315
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:02,002
It's okay.

316
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:04,213
Mariela?

317
00:16:05,631 --> 00:16:06,715
Bea?

318
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:12,179
Oh, what happened here?

319
00:16:12,262 --> 00:16:16,058
[LYDIA] Sis, let's just leave. Come on!

320
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:18,852
[PRECIOUS] Wait a second.

321
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:25,943
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

322
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:31,615
[PRECIOUS] Mariela?

323
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:46,463
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

324
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:53,429
[PHONE SHUTTERING]

325
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:58,892
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

326
00:16:58,976 --> 00:17:00,853
[MUSIC TURNS SUSPENSEFUL]

327
00:17:00,936 --> 00:17:02,938
- [PRECIOUS] Wait a second.
- [LYDIA] Someone's inside.

328
00:17:07,651 --> 00:17:09,153
[LYDIA] Let's get going.

329
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:10,654
Let's get out of here.

330
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:12,406
[MARIELA] What are you doing here?

331
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:18,662
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

332
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:20,330
Mariela.

333
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:23,000
Mariela, what happened to you?

334
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:25,002
I was cooking.

335
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:26,712
[MARIELA] I got hurt.

336
00:17:26,795 --> 00:17:28,172
But I asked you,

337
00:17:28,255 --> 00:17:30,299
what are you doing here?

338
00:17:30,382 --> 00:17:34,219
Mariela, I just came here to clarify
what you said earlier.

339
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:36,764
Were you referring to me and Billy?

340
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:39,183
So what if I was?

341
00:17:39,266 --> 00:17:41,810
You're threatening to kill us?

342
00:17:41,894 --> 00:17:45,606
People who deceive and steal

343
00:17:46,231 --> 00:17:48,067
deserve to die.

344
00:17:48,650 --> 00:17:50,027
Did we deceive you?

345
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:51,403
[PRECIOUS] Did we steal from you?

346
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:54,531
And what's the deal with
Billy's pictures upstairs?

347
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:56,658
When has Billy ever wronged you?

348
00:17:56,742 --> 00:17:59,703
Billy's not the only one who wronged us.

349
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:03,040
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

350
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:04,500
You've wronged us too.

351
00:18:05,542 --> 00:18:08,045
Mariela, what are you even talking about?

352
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:10,714
I will fight for our rights!

353
00:18:10,798 --> 00:18:13,550
What rights are you
even talking about, Mariela?

354
00:18:13,634 --> 00:18:16,261
[MARIELA] I won't let me or
my daughter get wronged again!

355
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:18,555
- Damn you!
- Stop that!

356
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:20,599
- Mariela, stop that!
- Mariela!

357
00:18:20,682 --> 00:18:22,309
- This is for my daughter!
- [LYDIA] Enough!

358
00:18:22,392 --> 00:18:23,852
- Mariela!
- You bastards!

359
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:27,564
- Damn you!
- [men] That's enough! Stop!

360
00:18:28,315 --> 00:18:30,776
[MARIELA] Just you wait!
I will come back for you!

361
00:18:30,859 --> 00:18:32,361
I will kill you!

362
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:33,529
You bastards!

363
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:36,073
Damn you all!

364
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:39,159
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

365
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:40,536
Are you all right?

366
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:46,416
You saw how happy
he was earlier, didn't you?

367
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:53,924
Didn't I tell you
that decision was for Oliver?

368
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:55,759
But is it the right choice?

369
00:18:56,343 --> 00:18:59,930
Well, we'll never know unless we try.

370
00:19:01,932 --> 00:19:03,058
[DOOR OPENING]

371
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:04,726
Okay then. Bye-bye.

372
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:05,644
[BILLY] Auntie Pres.

373
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:08,397
Are you all right?

374
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:11,150
Did you get to talk with Ms. Mariela?

375
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:15,529
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

376
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:24,872
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

377
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:48,854
["ABELYANA" BY MAKI PLAYING]

378
00:19:59,114 --> 00:20:05,954
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

379
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:27,976
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

380
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:37,027
<i>Auntie Pres, even if you were trespassing,</i>
<i>what she did was still wrong!</i>

381
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:39,279
<i>We should report her!</i>
<i>You got hurt.</i>

382
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,657
[PRECIOUS] <i>We were shocked</i>
<i>when we saw that there.</i>

383
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:44,618
[WOMAN] <i>Your mother</i>
<i>almost murdered someone!</i>

384
00:20:44,701 --> 00:20:49,539
<i>Now I understand why you're</i>
<i>so furious at that Billy!</i>

385
00:20:49,623 --> 00:20:50,958
[BEA]<i> I will avenge us.</i>

386
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:54,920
<i>I will avenge us both, okay?</i>

387
00:20:55,003 --> 00:20:59,258
<i>Auntie, can we invite Papa</i>
<i>to my moving-up ceremony?</i>

388
00:20:59,841 --> 00:21:01,718
<i>I got high honors.</i>

389
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:03,220
[ENRICO] <i>Remember this, son.</i>

390
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:05,264
<i>From now on, I'll always be here for you.</i>

391
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:09,142
<i>You're right, Precious.</i>
<i>I deceived you.</i>

392
00:21:09,726 --> 00:21:11,687
<i>But the love I have for my children</i>

393
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:13,313
<i>and for you</i>

394
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:14,815
<i>is real.</i>

395
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:18,652
<i>Dude? Bea and her mother</i>
<i>are now gone.</i>

396
00:21:18,735 --> 00:21:21,113
<i>Isn't this better?</i>
<i>For them to just go away?</i>

397
00:21:21,196 --> 00:21:24,616
<i>If it were just about me,</i>
<i>fine, I'd let it slide.</i>

398
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,076
<i>But we're talking about Auntie Pres.</i>

399
00:21:26,159 --> 00:21:27,869
<i>I won't just let it go. Sorry.</i>

400
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:28,954
<i>I'm just worried about you.</i>

401
00:21:29,037 --> 00:21:35,502
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]
